20972-       Thumb supports four types of Load and Store Multiple instructions:
20973-
20974-       � Two instructions, LDMIA and STMIA, are designed to support block copy. They have a fixed Increment
20975-               After addressing mode from a base register.
20976-
20977:       � The other two instructions, PUSH and POP, also have a fixed addressing mode. They implement a full
20978-               descending stack and the stack pointer (R13) is used as the base register.
20979-
20980-       All four instructions update the base register after transfer and all can transfer any or all of the lower 8
20981:       registers. PUSH can also stack the return address, and POP can load the PC.
20982-
20983-A6.6.1 Formats
20984-              Load and Store Multiple instructions have the following formats:
20985-
20986-       Format 1
--
20992-
20993-       1100L                          Rn                                        register_list
20994-
20995-       Format 2
20996-
20997:       PUSH {<registers>}
20998:       POP {<registers>}
20999-
21000-       15 14 13 12 11 10 9 8 7                                                                 0
21001-
21002-       1 0 1 1L1 0R                                                             register_list
21003-
