24328-
24329:PUSH (Push Multiple Registers) stores a subset (or possibly all) of the general-purpose registers R0-R7 and
24330-the LR to the stack.
24331-
24332-Syntax            Is the list of registers to be stored, separated by commas and surrounded by { and }.
24333-                  The list is encoded in the register_list field of the instruction, by setting bit[i] to 1 if
24334:PUSH <registers>  register Ri is included in the list and to 0 otherwise, for each of i=0 to 7. The R bit
24335-                  (bit[8]) is set to 1 if the LR is in the list and to 0 otherwise.
24336-where:
24337-                  At least one register must be stored. If bits[8:0] are all zero, the result is
24338-<registers>       UNPREDICTABLE.
