24400-       For details on shared memory and synchronization primitives, see Synchronization primitives on
24401-       page A2-44.
24402-
24403-       Usage
24404-
24405:       Use PUSH for stack operations. A PUSH instruction with the LR in the register list can be used for an efficient
24406-       procedure entry, as it saves registers (including the return address) on the stack and updates the stack pointer
24407:       with a single instruction. A matching POP instruction can be used later to return from the procedure.
24408-
