26656-B2.2.3 Memory synchronization primitives
--
28093-A (bit[1])     In ARM architecture v6, this controls strict alignment:
28094-               0 = Alignment not strict
28095-               1 = Strict alignment. If a data access is not aligned to the width of the accessed data item, a
28096-               Data Abort exception is generated.
28097-               In architectures before v6, for memory systems which optionally allow the alignment of data
28098:               memory accesses to be checked, this bit enables and disables alignment fault checking:
28099:               0 = Alignment fault checking disabled
28100:               1 = Alignment fault checking enabled.
28101-               For other memory systems, this bit ignores writes, and reads as 1 or 0 according to whether
28102-               the memory system does or does not check the alignment of data memory accesses.
28103-
28104-C (bit[2])     If a L1 unified cache is used, this is the enable/disable bit for the unified cache. If separate
28105-               L1 caches are used, this is the enable/disable bit for the data cache. In either case:
--
