The two edits are present at lines 1673 and 1867. The seven remaining calls are SWP/SWPB, LDREX/STREX, and instruction fetch; they are not ordinary generated loads/stores.

Two qualifications matter: the manual conditions word rounding on the alignment-control settings, and this `memory_rw.c` already splits translated transfers at 1 KB boundaries. I’m checking how that affects faults and whether combined LDM/STM handlers still bypass the corrected helpers.
