4749: 		/*
4750: 		 *  Check for availability of optimized implementation:
4751: 		 *  xxxx100P USWLnnnn llllllll llllllll
4752: 		 *           ^  ^ ^ ^        ^  ^ ^ ^   (0x00950154)
4753: 		 *  These bits are used to select which list to scan, and then
4754: 		 *  the list is scanned linearly.
4755: 		 *
4756: 		 *  The optimized functions do not support show_trace_tree,
4757: 		 *  but it's ok to use the unoptimized version in that case.
4758: 		 *
4759: 		 *  #378: nor do they support a big-endian guest -- the emitted
4760: 		 *  bodies move raw host words (generate_arm_multi.c has no
4761: 		 *  byte-order term), so on this LE host a BE guest's LDM/STM
4762: 		 *  through them is byte-reversed per word, and 23 of the 256
4763: 		 *  handlers load PC, i.e. a reversed RETURN ADDRESS. bdt_load/
4764: 		 *  bdt_store (via arm_pop/arm_push) swap on both their warm and
4765: 		 *  cold arms, so installing only for a little-endian guest makes
4766: 		 *  every BE multi-transfer correct at the cost of the fast path
4767: 		 *  no BE guest today can boot to use. Resolving the guest term
4768: 		 *  at translate time is sound because cpu->byte_order cannot
4769: 		 *  change after translation: every write is machine-setup-time,
4770: 		 *  SETEND is undecoded (and ARM_FLAG_E inert), and the CP15 c1
4771: 		 *  B-bit route exits the emulator (see cpu_arm_coproc.c). The
4772: 		 *  same decision the MIPS multi generator makes with its _le/_be
4773: 		 *  variants -- a future BE-ARM-guest round should emit those
4774: 		 *  (S4 in the round-119/#378 records) rather than re-open this
4775: 		 *  gate. NOTE the memcpy fold's two BAIL-OUT calls also invoke
