19716:                             locations accessed, lying at the top (U==0) or bottom (U==1) of that range.
19717: 
19718:                       P==1  indicates that the word addressed by Rn is excluded from the range of memory
19719:                             locations accessed, and lies one word beyond the top of the range (U==0) or one
19720:                             word below the bottom of the range (U==1).
19721: 
19722:        The U bit      Indicates that the transfer is made upwards (U==1) or downwards (U==0) from the base
19723:                       register.
19724: 
19725:        The S bit      For LDMs that load the PC, the S bit indicates that the CPSR is loaded from the SPSR. For
