19942: 
19943: Stack operations
19944: 
19945: Load Multiple and Store Multiple addressing modes can be specified with an alternative syntax, which is
19946: more applicable to stack operations:
19947: 
19948: Full stacks       Have stack pointers that point to the last used (full) location.
19949: 
19950: Empty stacks      Have stack pointers that point to the first unused (empty) location.
19951: 
19952: Descending stacks Grow towards decreasing memory addresses (towards the bottom of memory).
19953: 
19954: Ascending stacks Grow towards increasing memory addresses (towards the top of memory).
19955: 
19956: Two attributes allow four types of stack to be defined:
19957: � Full Descending, with the syntax FD
19958: � Empty Descending, with the syntax ED
19959: � Full Ascending, with the syntax FA
