codex
I found two remaining unaligned LDM/STM access paths in the permitted file: the combined `netbsd_memset` and `netbsd_memcpy` handlers use raw byte offsets. Their matchers do not check address alignment, and their combined bodies bypass the two edited calls.

So the edits cover both generic slow-transfer sites, but a search for `memory_rw` calls alone misses other implementations of the same word-rounding rule. I also cannot name a failing row in the shipped detector: none of the permitted files contains its row inventory.
