30154: B4.9.7 Register 6: Fault Address register
30155:               This register enables the data and watchpoint Fault Address registers to be accessed, depending on the value
30156:               of the Opcode2 field, as shown in Table B4-4. Prior to VMSAv6, only a combined FAR was defined.
30157: 
30158:                                                                                              Table B4-4 Fault Address registers
30159: 
30160:                                     Register name                                 Opcode2
30161:                                                                                   0
30162:                                     Combined/Data FAR                             1
30163:                                     Watchpoint FAR (WFAR)                         2
30164:                                     Instruction FAR (IFAR):
30165:                                     optional
30166: 
30167:        The FAR, WFAR, and IFAR are updated on an abort in accordance with Table B4-2 on page B4-22.
30168: 
30169:                 Note
30170:        The contents of the WFAR are a virtual address, not a Modified Virtual Address (MVA). The FAR and IFAR
30171:        contain a MVA where the FCSE mechanism is in use (see Modified virtual addresses on page B8-3).
30172: 
30173:        The WFAR feature is migrating from CP15 to the debug architecture in CP14 and as such decoding the
30174:        WFAR through CP15 is deprecated in ARMv6. See Coprocessor 14 debug registers on page D3-2 for its
30175:        revised location.
30176: 
30177:        The IFAR is optional in VMSAv6 and mandated for PMSAv6. It is only updated on prefetch aborts.
30178: 
30179:        Writing CP15 register 6 enables the values of the FAR, IFAR, and WFAR to be written. This is useful for a
30180:        debugger to restore their values. When the FAR is written by an MCR instruction, its value is treated as data,
30181:        and no address modification is performed by the FCSE.
