The page-fault answer is yes: for a four-byte access starting in a page’s last three bytes, the old call could reach the next mapping; the rounded call stays within the current page. Removing that extra access is part of correcting the word selection.

The manual also makes ARMv6 unaligned Device/Strongly Ordered transfers UNPREDICTABLE and requires alignment faults in other control modes. I’ll make those limits explicit, alongside the unresolved Thumb-dispatch and detector-score checks.
